{
 "id": "page-deployment-log-science",
 "target": "page",
 "page": "deployment-log.html",
 "goal": "On the deployment log: a 48 kHz recorder records up to 24 kHz and cannot survey bats, 192 kHz covers most of it, 384 kHz all; a 60 s in 600 s duty over 14 days at 16-bit mono 48 kHz writes 11.61 GB (10.0%, 33.6 h) and a 32 GB card lasts 39 days, 300/3600 over 30 days 20.74 GB, 60/60 over 7 days 58.06 GB, and 600/600 over 30 days (248.83 GB) fills an 8 GB card; clock drift at 1 s/day is 343 m of sound per day (10.3 km at 30 days); GSD = sensor width x altitude / (focal length x image width): RedEdge 4.17/8.33, P4 3.18/6.36, Sequoia 5.65/11.31 cm/px at 60/120 m; 70/60 overlap is below Pix4D, 85/85 meets it; a logger at 600 s over 90 days takes 12,960 readings and 84,650 memory fills after 588 days, at 60 s over 30 days with 20,000 it fills after 14 days; a logged recorder lands in the table and the .eco export. Then the log's field sheet is read: Copy field sheet hands over the whole sheet byte for byte — three deployments, the flight's GSD 2.10 cm/px at 120 m, the logger every 1 min for 90 d, the recorder at 48 kHz mono with Nyquist 24.0 kHz — and the print button prints.",
